# [Project Name] — Developer Onboarding

> Start here if you are new to this project. This document orients you to the system, tooling, and standards before your first contribution.

---

## First 30 Minutes

1. **Read `context.md`** — understand what this project is and its current state.
2. **Read `domain.md`** — learn the terminology the team uses.
3. **Read `data-model.md`** — understand the schema and naming conventions.
4. **Clone the repository** and set up your local environment (see below).
5. **Create your `.ai_local/` directory** locally — this is your personal working memory, never committed.

---

## Repository Setup

```bash
# Clone the repo
git clone [repo URL]
cd [repo-directory]

# Verify .ai_local/ is in .gitignore
grep ".ai_local" .gitignore

# Create your personal context directory
mkdir .ai_local
mkdir .ai_local/session-summaries
```

